    "title": "Beautiful Towers II",
    "category": "Stack",
    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "problemStatement": "You are given the maximum allowed heights of n towers. Construct the heights of all towers such that: Each height is at least 1. Each height does not exceed its maximum allowed height. Heights are non-increasing as you move away from a chosen peak. Return the maximum possible sum of all tower heights. Unlike the previous version, this problem requires an efficient solution for much larger input sizes.",
    "input": "Integer n Array maxHeights",
    "output": "A single integer.",
    "constraints": "1 <= n <= 2 \u00d7 10^5 1 <= maxHeights[i] <= 10^9"
